{
  "title": "WebShop: Towards Scalable Real-World Web Interaction with Grounded Language Agents",
  "authors": [
    "Shunyu Yao",
    "Howard Chen",
    "John Yang",
    "Karthik Narasimhan"
  ],
  "year": 2023,
  "arxivId": "2207.01206",
  "abstract": "WebShop is a simulated e-commerce website environment that enables the development of grounded language models. It consists of 1.18 million real-world products and 12,087 crowd-sourced text instructions, allowing agents to navigate multiple types of webpages and issue diverse actions to find, customize, and purchase an item. The environment provides several challenges for language grounding, including understanding compositional instructions, query reformulation, and strategic exploration.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "The WebShop environment is designed to simulate real-world web interaction with grounded language agents. It <strong>combines natural language processing and reinforcement learning</strong> to enable agents to navigate multiple types of webpages and issue diverse actions to find, customize, and purchase an item. The environment <strong>provides several challenges for language grounding</strong>, including understanding compositional instructions, query reformulation, and strategic exploration.",
